# Lockfiles are owned by npm, not by this project's style
package-lock.json

# Untracked scratch space. `.probe/` holds the one-off scripts and JSON dumps the M1/M2 specs were
# derived from; `.claude/` holds local agent config and worktrees. Neither is committed, so neither
# should be able to fail `format:check` in CI.
#
# The probes a review cites are not scratch — they are committed under `tools/probe/` and are
# formatted like the rest of the tracked tree, so a reader can re-run the claim and `format:check`
# still covers it. Only the uncommitted `.probe/` is ignored here.
/.probe/
/.claude/

# The corpus harness's own output, rewritten by every run (mirrors .gitignore). `npm run
# format:check` gates CI, so a generated file that churns per run must not be able to fail it.
#
# `CHURN.md` is generated Markdown full of diff excerpts whose content is quoted Motoko; running the
# repo's own formatter over it would try to format code fences that are deliberately unformatted,
# and would rewrite the file that the next run overwrites anyway.
/tools/corpus/report.json
/tools/corpus/RESULTS.md
/tools/corpus/CHURN.md

# Machine-generated zero-width character table (~1.5k lines, reformatting it is pure churn)
src/utils/removeZeroWidthCharacters.json
